cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Aegis, please cite it as below."
title: "Aegis: honest error bars for portfolio risk"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mishra
    given-names: Priyanshu
repository-code: "https://github.com/priyanshu-mishra/aegis"
url: "https://priyanshu-mishra.github.io/aegis/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A walk-forward study of conformal prediction for market risk. Volatility and Value-at-Risk
  forecasts for a four-ETF portfolio are wrapped in adaptive conformal intervals and audited on
  1,712 unseen trading days (2020-2026), against five classical baselines, with Kupiec,
  Christoffersen, Acerbi-Szekely and Basel tests.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - value at risk
  - expected shortfall
  - volatility forecasting
  - model validation
